Rule 2 (input integral when other is integer scalar; shift count non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∧ (v_2 ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 3 (broadcasting compatibility between input and other tensors; suppresses size-mismatch error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : (ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
>>
Rule 4 (out must be a tensor of integral dtype; suppresses "out=float" TypeError and cast to Half)
{v_3 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 6 (out dtype aligns with one of the input dtypes for tensor-tensor; suppresses unsafe cast errors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) ∨ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_2)) ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≤ 5
